[{"text": "I now give the floor to his excellency", "start": 1.36, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "Abdul Khad Hussein Omar, Minister of", "start": 4.24, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "Foreign Affairs and International", "start": 7.04, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "Cooperation, government spokesperson of", "start": 8.639, "duration": 5.481}, {"text": "Djibouti", "start": 11.12, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "At the outset, I should like to convey", "start": 37.68, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "to this August assembly the greetings of", "start": 41.84, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "his excellency Ismael Omar Gle,", "start": 44.0, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "President of the Republic of Djibouti.", "start": 46.96, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "Mr. President, allow me on behalf of the", "start": 49.92, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "Republic of Djibouti to extend my warm", "start": 52.399, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "congratulations to his excellency Mr.", "start": 55.36, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "Khalil Rahman of Bangladesh on his", "start": 57.28, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "election as president of the 81st", "start": 60.16, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "session of the United Nations General", "start": 63.6, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "Assembly and to wish him every success", "start": 65.92, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "in carrying out his mandate. I would", "start": 68.64, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "also like to pay tribute to her", "start": 71.76, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "excellency", "start": 73.68, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "Madame Analena Berbach for her", "start": 75.52, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "leadership during the last session which", "start": 77.84, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "marked the 80th anniversary of our", "start": 80.24, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "organization.", "start": 82.64, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "The Republic of Djibouti welcomes the", "start": 84.32, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "choice of the theme for this session,", "start": 86.56, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "restoring trust, managing", "start": 89.04, "duration": 4.079}, {"text": "transformation,", "start": 91.6, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "a united nations that delivers for all.", "start": 93.119, "duration": 8.161}, {"text": "This theme is particularly relevant", "start": 98.0, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "In the current international context,", "start": 101.28, "duration": 5.119}, {"text": "we're living through a critical juncture", "start": 104.24, "duration": 4.559}, {"text": "exacerbated by the proliferation of", "start": 106.399, "duration": 4.241}, {"text": "conflicts,", "start": 108.799, "duration": 4.241}, {"text": "deepening existing crises and the", "start": 110.64, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "emergence of conflicts", "start": 113.04, "duration": 5.759}, {"text": "and the emergence of new crises with", "start": 116.32, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "devastating political, economic,", "start": 118.799, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "humanitarian and security consequences.", "start": 120.88, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "In the face of these challenges, we must", "start": 124.479, "duration": 4.161}, {"text": "reaffirm the essential mission of the", "start": 126.479, "duration": 6.641}, {"text": "United Nations and strengthen a renewed,", "start": 128.64, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "more inclusive, and more effective", "start": 133.12, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "multilateralism that takes full account", "start": 134.8, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "of the interests of all states, large", "start": 137.44, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "and small.", "start": 139.599, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "The region that is home to my country", "start": 142.8, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "also continues to face crises, the", "start": 145.28, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "consequences of which extend beyond our", "start": 148.56, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "national borders. Djibouti is following", "start": 150.72, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "the situation in Yemen with grave", "start": 154.4, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "concern.", "start": 156.319, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "We are indeed directly experiencing its", "start": 158.16, "duration": 4.719}, {"text": "effects with the recent arrival in our", "start": 160.72, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "territory of several thousand people", "start": 162.879, "duration": 4.161}, {"text": "fleeing the violence.", "start": 164.8, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "This situation is already placing", "start": 167.04, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "considerable pressure on host", "start": 170.64, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "communities in the Obok region as well", "start": 172.08, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "as on the reception capacity of the", "start": 175.28, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "Marazai site. Djibouti alone cannot meet", "start": 177.68, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "the growing needs for shelter, food, and", "start": 181.76, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "essential services.", "start": 184.0, "duration": 4.319}, {"text": "Therefore, we reiterate our appeal to", "start": 186.159, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "the international community to step up", "start": 188.319, "duration": 6.401}, {"text": "its support so that we can respond", "start": 190.959, "duration": 7.92}, {"text": "adequately to this influx, which", "start": 194.72, "duration": 6.799}, {"text": "according to UN estimates could reach up", "start": 198.879, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "to 10,000 people. In order to prevent", "start": 201.519, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "this humanitarian crisis from becoming", "start": 204.8, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "protracted, we renew our call for", "start": 207.2, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "deescalation and for a lasting political", "start": 210.4, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "solution in Yemen to preserve human", "start": 212.72, "duration": 6.879}, {"text": "life. Turning now to Somalia, we remain", "start": 214.48, "duration": 7.92}, {"text": "fully committed to the Somali people and", "start": 219.599, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "government in their quest to consolidate", "start": 222.4, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "peace and stability. The international", "start": 225.12, "duration": 3.839}, {"text": "community must preserve the security", "start": 227.28, "duration": 3.36}, {"text": "gains that have been made and continue", "start": 228.959, "duration": 3.681}, {"text": "to support the Somali authorities in", "start": 230.64, "duration": 4.159}, {"text": "fully shouldering their responsibilities", "start": 232.64, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "and protecting their institutions.", "start": 234.799, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "In this regard, we recognize the crucial", "start": 237.36, "duration": 6.239}, {"text": "role played by AUM in stabilizing the", "start": 239.519, "duration": 6.241}, {"text": "country as well as the crucial support", "start": 243.599, "duration": 3.761}, {"text": "provided by the United Nations,", "start": 245.76, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "particularly through ANSOS.", "start": 247.36, "duration": 4.879}, {"text": "We hope that the international community", "start": 249.68, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "will stand mobilized so as to enable", "start": 252.239, "duration": 6.161}, {"text": "Somalis to", "start": 254.959, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "assume lasting responsibility for their", "start": 258.4, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "security, sovereignty and the", "start": 260.639, "duration": 4.321}, {"text": "preservation of the integrity of their", "start": 262.16, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "national territory.", "start": 264.96, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "Turning now to Sudan. Djibouti in its", "start": 267.759, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "capacity as current chair of IAD", "start": 270.8, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "welcomes the return of that kindred", "start": 273.68, "duration": 4.239}, {"text": "country to full participation on our", "start": 276.08, "duration": 3.28}, {"text": "regional organization of which is a", "start": 277.919, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "founding member. We call for", "start": 279.36, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "deescalation and the resumption of talks", "start": 283.52, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "to be prioritized. Only an inclusive", "start": 285.6, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "political solution that places the Sudin", "start": 287.919, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "people at the heart of every initiative", "start": 290.16, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "will make it possible to restore lasting", "start": 292.8, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "peace and stability. We also call on", "start": 295.68, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "foreign actors to refrain from fueling", "start": 298.32, "duration": 7.08}, {"text": "this war through harmful interference.", "start": 300.479, "duration": 4.921}, {"text": "Once again, we extend a hand to our", "start": 305.52, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "Eratrayan neighbor. Djibouti remains", "start": 307.759, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "convinced that dialogue and negotiation", "start": 310.4, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "in full respect for international law", "start": 312.479, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "represent the only path towards a", "start": 315.039, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "peaceful and definitive settlement of", "start": 317.28, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "our border dispute and the return of our", "start": 320.08, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "prisoners of war who have been held in", "start": 323.199, "duration": 7.761}, {"text": "communicado for more than 18 years.", "start": 326.16, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "The Republic of Djibouti further", "start": 330.96, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "reaffirms its unwavering solidarity with", "start": 332.8, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "the Palestinian people and its full", "start": 334.96, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "support for their legitimate rights, in", "start": 337.44, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "particular their inalienable right to", "start": 340.24, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "the establishment of an independent and", "start": 342.56, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "sovereign state. We reaffirm our", "start": 345.12, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "commitment to a two-state solution based", "start": 348.08, "duration": 7.44}, {"text": "on the 1967 borders with East Jerusalem", "start": 351.28, "duration": 7.199}, {"text": "as the capital of the state of Palestine", "start": 355.52, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "as the path towards a a just and lasting", "start": 358.479, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "peace. We roundly condemn", "start": 361.28, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "illegal settlement activity, violence", "start": 365.039, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "committed against civilians, including", "start": 367.6, "duration": 4.319}, {"text": "by Israeli settlers in the West Bank,", "start": 369.919, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "force displacement placement, and any", "start": 371.919, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "policy aimed at altering the demographic", "start": 374.639, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "and territorial reality of the occupied", "start": 377.039, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "Palestinian territory. The humanitarian", "start": 379.6, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "situation in Gaza remains a tragedy,", "start": 382.72, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "requiring an immediate response from the", "start": 385.28, "duration": 3.759}, {"text": "international community. The protection", "start": 386.88, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "of civilians must be guaranteed.", "start": 389.039, "duration": 4.241}, {"text": "Humanitarian assistance must reach those", "start": 390.8, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "in need without hindrance", "start": 393.28, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "and violations of international", "start": 395.759, "duration": 4.321}, {"text": "humanitarian law must cease and be", "start": 397.6, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "condemned.", "start": 400.08, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "Djibouti will continue to support", "start": 402.96, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "efforts to bring an end to the suffering", "start": 405.28, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "of the Palestinian people and to ensure", "start": 407.68, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "that justice, peace, and international", "start": 410.88, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "law prevail.", "start": 412.88, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "Preserving freedom of navigation in the", "start": 415.36, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "Red Sea and more particularly through", "start": 417.52, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "the Baba Mandde Strait is a major", "start": 419.759, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "geopolitical and economic issue for", "start": 422.72, "duration": 6.84}, {"text": "regional and global stability.", "start": 425.12, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "This strategic maritime passage is a", "start": 430.319, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "vital artery for international trade and", "start": 432.639, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "any obstruction to free movement of", "start": 434.72, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "shipping could seriously affect supply", "start": 437.599, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "chains and energy security.", "start": 440.639, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "Although Djibouti has observed no", "start": 443.28, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "disruption to passage through the strait", "start": 445.599, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "to date, my country's authorities remain", "start": 447.84, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "particularly watchful with regard to the", "start": 451.199, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "current tensions affecting the region.", "start": 453.36, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "Mr. President, the climate emergency is", "start": 456.24, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "one of the most pressing challenges", "start": 458.56, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "facing our international community. For", "start": 460.08, "duration": 7.92}, {"text": "Djibouti, as an African coastal country,", "start": 463.84, "duration": 6.639}, {"text": "this emergency is indivisible from", "start": 468.0, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "development. Rising sea levels pose a", "start": 470.479, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "direct and growing threat to our", "start": 474.08, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "populations and ecosystems.", "start": 476.08, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "Djibouti, like many developing", "start": 478.8, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "countries, makes only a marginal", "start": 480.479, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "contribution to global emissions, yet", "start": 482.96, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "remains particularly exposed to the", "start": 485.44, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "consequences of climate disruption.", "start": 487.68, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "This situation highlights a profound", "start": 490.72, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "injustice. Those countries that have", "start": 492.8, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "contributed least to climate change are", "start": 494.72, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "often those that suffer its most severe", "start": 496.56, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "consequences. We must therefore", "start": 499.199, "duration": 3.921}, {"text": "accelerate the implementation of the", "start": 501.599, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "Paris Agreement and strengthen our", "start": 503.12, "duration": 5.759}, {"text": "adaptation and resilience efforts,", "start": 505.199, "duration": 6.641}, {"text": "including through", "start": 508.879, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "resilient coastal infrastructure,", "start": 511.84, "duration": 4.879}, {"text": "better protection for marine and coastal", "start": 514.479, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "ecosystems,", "start": 516.719, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "early warning systems, and simplified,", "start": 518.479, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "predictable, and equitable access to", "start": 520.959, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "climate finance.", "start": 522.88, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "For Djibouti, climate action must not be", "start": 525.76, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "separated from development. On the", "start": 528.08, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "contrary, it must help to transform our", "start": 529.76, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "economies,", "start": 532.24, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "develop renewable energy, create jobs,", "start": 533.76, "duration": 5.759}, {"text": "and open up new opportunities for", "start": 536.56, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "investment and innovation.", "start": 539.519, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "And it's in this spirit that the", "start": 542.959, "duration": 3.281}, {"text": "government is working to operationalize", "start": 544.32, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "the mechanisms provided for under", "start": 546.24, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "article six of the Paris agreement", "start": 548.32, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "through a robust, transparent and", "start": 550.56, "duration": 4.719}, {"text": "credible national framework for carbon", "start": 553.04, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "markets with a view to mobilizing new", "start": 555.279, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "resources, attracting investment,", "start": 558.24, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "promoting technology transfer and", "start": 560.959, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "strengthening national capacities.", "start": 563.12, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "This transformation however requires", "start": 566.959, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "resources. Developing countries continue", "start": 569.04, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "to face high financing costs, external", "start": 571.36, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "vulnerabilities, and limited fiscal", "start": 574.0, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "space.", "start": 575.92, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "Access to climate finance and reform of", "start": 578.08, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "the international financial architecture", "start": 580.48, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "therefore remain essential.", "start": 583.2, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "In this regard, the SEIA commitment", "start": 586.72, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "represents an important step forward", "start": 589.04, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "whose commitments must now be translated", "start": 591.04, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "into tangible results, including through", "start": 593.04, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "improved access to concessional", "start": 596.56, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "financing, enhanced debt sustainability,", "start": 598.32, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "and increased mobilization of public and", "start": 601.12, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "private capital for development.", "start": 603.44, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "We must also strengthen South South and", "start": 606.48, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "triangular cooperation in order to share", "start": 608.72, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "technologies, knowledge and solutions", "start": 611.2, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "tailored to the realities of our", "start": 614.56, "duration": 3.519}, {"text": "countries.", "start": 616.0, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "Africa must not be viewed solely as a", "start": 618.079, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "region vulnerable to climate change. It", "start": 621.519, "duration": 4.081}, {"text": "should be recognized as an actor that is", "start": 623.76, "duration": 3.759}, {"text": "capable of innovating, proposing", "start": 625.6, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "solutions, and contributing to the", "start": 627.519, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "transformation of the global economy.", "start": 630.24, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "Beyond climate action, the 2030 agenda", "start": 632.16, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "remains at the heart of our development", "start": 634.88, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "vision. Djibouti's economy is", "start": 636.8, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "demonstrating resilience driven in", "start": 639.6, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "particular by port logistics activities,", "start": 642.24, "duration": 5.839}, {"text": "trade, telecommunications, energy, and", "start": 645.68, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "investment.", "start": 648.079, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "Djibouti intends to consolidate its role", "start": 650.64, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "as a regional hub while", "start": 653.279, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "accelerating the diversification of our", "start": 656.16, "duration": 5.0}, {"text": "economy.", "start": 658.16, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "This ambition can be seen just as", "start": 662.32, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "recently as this week with the launch of", "start": 664.24, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "construction work on modern petroleum", "start": 667.04, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "product storage facilities and transport", "start": 670.399, "duration": 4.321}, {"text": "infrastructure including oil and gas", "start": 672.64, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "pipelines in Djibouti linking Djibouti", "start": 674.72, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "and Ethiopia. These projects illustrate", "start": 676.88, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "our ambition to achieve energy", "start": 679.6, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "sovereignty and security, regional", "start": 681.519, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "integration and economic transformation.", "start": 683.36, "duration": 4.719}, {"text": "But above all, growth should translate", "start": 686.16, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "into jobs, social progress, and", "start": 688.079, "duration": 3.2}, {"text": "opportunities, particularly for women", "start": 689.76, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "and young people. We are continuing to", "start": 691.279, "duration": 6.841}, {"text": "invest in education, health,", "start": 693.68, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "and to achieve the sustainable", "start": 700.56, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "development goals and implement the", "start": 702.88, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "African Union's agenda 2063.", "start": 704.88, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "Both require a collective surge of", "start": 708.079, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "action. The climate emergency demands", "start": 710.32, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "action. Development demands investment", "start": 712.72, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "and peace and humanitarian crisis", "start": 715.68, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "demands solidarity.", "start": 718.0, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "The digital transition and artificial", "start": 720.48, "duration": 3.52}, {"text": "intelligence also offer new", "start": 722.32, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "opportunities to accelerate development", "start": 724.0, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "and improve the capacities of our", "start": 726.24, "duration": 3.839}, {"text": "states.", "start": 728.56, "duration": 3.04}, {"text": "Their", "start": 730.079, "duration": 4.241}, {"text": "potential, however, will only be fully", "start": 731.6, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "realized if we're able to bridge the", "start": 734.32, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "digital divide, facilitate technology", "start": 736.48, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "sharing, and build the capacities of", "start": 738.72, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "developing countries.", "start": 741.6, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "And with that in mind, Djibouti supports", "start": 743.68, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "the beyond GDP intergovernmental", "start": 746.32, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "process. This seeks to complement", "start": 750.16, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "traditional economic indicators with", "start": 752.16, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "measures that better take into account", "start": 754.16, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "people's well-being, social inclusion,", "start": 756.32, "duration": 7.92}, {"text": "and environmental sustainability.", "start": 759.519, "duration": 7.44}, {"text": "Djibouti supports efforts to adapt the", "start": 764.24, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "UN to contemporary challenges and", "start": 766.959, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "enhance its effectiveness.", "start": 769.44, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "But we must make it clear that our", "start": 771.92, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "organization does not exist merely to", "start": 773.839, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "balance the books.", "start": 777.44, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "Rather, it is here to serve our peoples", "start": 780.079, "duration": 4.081}, {"text": "and to give effect to the decisions that", "start": 782.16, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "we take together.", "start": 784.16, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "Any reform should continue to be guided", "start": 787.12, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "by the mandates established by member", "start": 789.44, "duration": 3.519}, {"text": "states and should preserve the balance", "start": 791.2, "duration": 3.52}, {"text": "between the three pillars, peace and", "start": 792.959, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "security, development and human rights.", "start": 794.72, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "As the mandate of the outgoing secretary", "start": 798.24, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "general, his excellency Antonio Gutes", "start": 800.56, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "draws to a close, I should like on", "start": 802.88, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "behalf of my president, his excellency", "start": 805.2, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "Ishmael Omar Gule to express our", "start": 807.279, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "profound gratitude for his years of", "start": 810.56, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "service to the UN. We wish him every", "start": 812.32, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "success and we sincerely thank him for", "start": 815.68, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "his invaluable contribution to global", "start": 818.48, "duration": 7.44}, {"text": "peace and justice.", "start": 822.24, "duration": 6.719}, {"text": "Finally, we are following very closely", "start": 825.92, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "the process to identify the most", "start": 828.959, "duration": 4.161}, {"text": "qualified person to serve as the next", "start": 831.04, "duration": 6.039}, {"text": "secretary general of the UN.", "start": 833.12, "duration": 3.959}, {"text": "That selection must be guided by", "start": 837.36, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "competence, professional integrity and", "start": 840.48, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "unequivocal commitment to respect for", "start": 842.56, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "international law and the ability", "start": 844.72, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "rigorously to implement the reforms on", "start": 847.04, "duration": 4.239}, {"text": "which member states have collectively", "start": 849.36, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "agreed. Thank you.", "start": 851.279, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "I thank the Minister of Foreign Affairs", "start": 857.76, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "and International Cooperation,", "start": 859.839, "duration": 7.161}, {"text": "government's uh spokesperson of Djibouti", "start": 861.6, "duration": 5.4}]